      },
      "transcriptionStatus": "source-verified",
      "gradingStatus": "official key verified",
      "hasFigure": false,
      "solution": "“Back out” means withdraw from an arrangement or plan. The injury makes the speaker withdraw from the skiing plan. The other phrasal forms do not convey that meaning here. Answer: D.",
      "solutionStatus": "independently checked editorial solution; not an official solution",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "answer": "D",
