      "transcriptionStatus": "source-verified",
      "gradingStatus": "official key verified",
      "hasFigure": false,
      "solution": "P costs ₹800/5=₹160 per kg and Q costs ₹800/4=₹200 per kg. An 8% profit at selling price ₹192 requires cost 192/1.08=₹1600/9 per kg. If weights are p and q, (160p+200q)/(p+q)=1600/9, hence 160p=200q and p:q=5:4. Answer: A.",
      "solutionStatus": "independently checked editorial solution; not an official solution",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "answer": "A",
