      "transcriptionStatus": "source-verified",
      "gradingStatus": "official key verified",
      "hasFigure": true,
      "solution": "The shortest connection is the perpendicular from P to QR. The triangle’s semiperimeter is (13+14+15)/2=21. By Heron’s formula its area is √(21×8×7×6)=84 km². Thus height=2×84/14=12 km; its foot lies on QR. Answer: C.",
